   disc host logM_b 10.5 canonical: r_M   6.86 kpc, V  147.8 km/s, settled cold <r_M 1.62e+10 Msun -> m_rlx 5.13e+05, m_df 1.34e+07 Msun
   disc host logM_b 10.5 alt      : r_M   6.25 kpc, V  155.0 km/s, settled cold <r_M 1.62e+10 Msun -> m_rlx 4.39e+05, m_df 1.17e+07 Msun
   disc host logM_b 11.5 canonical: r_M  21.70 kpc, V  262.9 km/s, settled cold <r_M 1.62e+11 Msun -> m_rlx 9.72e+06, m_df 2.39e+08 Msun
   disc host logM_b 11.5 alt      : r_M  19.75 kpc, V  275.6 km/s, settled cold <r_M 1.62e+11 Msun -> m_rlx 8.31e+06, m_df 2.07e+08 Msun
A3 smallest granularity mass 2.70e-01 Msun = 5.37e+32 g; above the window top (1e22 g) by 10.7 dex -> granularity IRRELEVANT in the window (PBHs there are a smooth collisionless fluid on every galactic scale)
   Relaxation as the settling MECHANISM would need m >= m_rlx, i.e. masses Part B excludes (UFD heating, dynamics): not available.
A4 settling routes open to PBHs: FL1 superfluid pressure NO (no pressure); CFG490 direct phonon coupling NO (a black hole
   carries no baryon/phonon charge; G9 holds automatically); CFG381 khronon +1 coupling ONLY via black-hole 'sensitivities' in
   khronometric gravity (recalled, NOT computed); two-body relaxation ONLY above m_rlx (excluded). PBHs have FEWER routes than a field.
PART A VERDICT: x1.82 -> DISAPPEARS CONDITIONALLY (settling postulate). Not RESOLVED: no settling mechanism is supplied on the record, and PBHs close two of its routes.

