PART B: f_PBH = 1 mass window (bands RECALLED, UNVERIFIED; no constraint curves on disk)
====================================================================================================
   open windows (robust): 1.02e+17 - 1.00e+22 g (4.99 dex)
   open windows (maximal): 4.07e+17 - 2.95e+21 g (3.86 dex)
   >= 1 dex window on BOTH sets: YES
D-checks (derived; a > 1 dex disagreement flags the band UNSUPPORTED BY DERIVATION, nothing is moved):
   D1 naive (photon-only 5120 pi) lifetime = 13.8 Gyr at M = 1.73e+14 g (recalled full-species value ~5e14 g);
      T_H(1e17 g) = 105.7 keV: emission today in hard X / soft gamma (511 keV, MeV), consistent with E1's edge being an
      EMISSION bound >> the lifetime mass. E1 edge not derivable without data: NO D-CHECK (stays recalled).
   D2 wave-optics edge (w = 8 pi G M/(c^2 lambda) = 1, r-band): 3.32e+22 g (+0.52 dex from E2's 1e22 g) -> supports E2's edge
      finite-source edge (R_E in source plane = R_sun): M31-halo lens 9.88e+25 g, MW-halo lens 1.83e+23 g
      (+1.3 dex above 1e22 g for Sun-size sources: the recalled edge needs sources smaller than the Sun or
      small-magnification detections; the derivation, if anything, WIDENS the window upward). E2 lower edge: SUPPORTED by wave
      optics, QUESTIONED by finite source -> flagged 'finite-source caveat'; scoring keeps the narrower recalled edge.
   D3 UFD star heating (record UFDs, real cold mass, lnL 10, 10 Gyr): median m_max 31.80 Msun (1-D sigma variant 6.12); most constraining [1.04, 2.5, 3.1] Msun; vs E5's 5 Msun: +0.80 dex -> SUPPORTED
   D4 LVK rate at f = 1 (recalled Sasaki-type 1.6e6 Gpc^-3/yr m^-32/37, x1e-3 suppression, also recalled): 1 Msun 1.6e+03, 10 Msun 2.2e+02, 30 Msun 8.4e+01, 100 Msun 3.0e+01, 300 Msun 1.2e+01 vs observed 17-45 (recalled)
      derived f=1 exclusion reaches only m <= 62 Msun (rate = 45); E8's 300 Msun edge is +0.68 dex beyond -> SUPPORTED within the 1-dex rule; the 1e-3 suppression factor dominates (rates
      at 30-300 Msun are within ~0.5 dex of observed). Above ~60 Msun E5/E6/E7/E9 cover the band anyway.
   D5 Poisson isocurvature at k = 0.05/Mpc, Delta^2_S / A_s: 1e+17 g 4.6e-24, 1e+20 g 4.6e-21, 1e+22 g 4.6e-19 -> utterly negligible (adiabatic on CMB scales)
