   -> near the low edge, the tail glows in 511 keV / MeV gamma rays (T_H ~ 100 keV at 1e17 g): COSI-class MeV data tests it.
   flybys: M 1e+17 g -> 2.2e+00 per yr within 1 AU; impulse at 1 AU 3.6e-13 m/s; displacement after 10 yr 1.1e-04 m
